WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:03.450
You might not have known
this but ancient Egypt

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:05.630
was an itchy place to live.

00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:06.773
Lice were rampant.

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:10.703
Cleopatra for example was buried
with solid gold lice combs,

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:14.190
while other Egyptians would
shave their entire bodies

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.510
to try and get rid of the parasites.

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:18.690
It's a problem we've had for a while,

00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:21.323
and we probably won't be
solving it anytime soon.

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.576
Humans and lice have been living together

00:00:25.576 --> 00:00:26.860
for about seven million years,

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:29.550
when our ancestors
first split from chimps,

00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:32.900
and we've been itching to
get rid of them ever since.

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:36.160
There are 532 species of lice out there,

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:36.993
but let's take a look

00:00:36.993 --> 00:00:39.340
at the most common type
that plagues humans:

00:00:39.340 --> 00:00:40.203
head lice.

00:00:41.540 --> 00:00:43.748
For starters, they have six legs,

00:00:43.748 --> 00:00:47.450
and each one has a tiny hook
at the end that helps them

00:00:47.450 --> 00:00:51.192
climb from one head to the
other, latch onto your hair,

00:00:51.192 --> 00:00:53.910
and quickly crawl down to your scalp

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:57.390
where they'll feast on your
blood several times a day.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.840
And once they've made
themselves comfortable,

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:02.310
lice are tricky to spot.

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:03.808
Adult lice, for example,

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.901
are about as large as a sesame seed.

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:10.473
While baby lice or nymphs
are a fraction of that size.

00:01:11.386 --> 00:01:14.210
Lice are well camouflaged, too,

00:01:14.210 --> 00:01:16.810
matching the color of
the hair around them.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:19.660
Not to mention your scalp is
the perfect breeding ground.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.563
In one day, a female louse
can lay up to eight eggs.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:27.160
Those eggs only take
about a week to hatch.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:28.600
Once they're 10 days old,

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:31.370
they'll start laying eggs of their own.

00:01:31.370 --> 00:01:34.850
While it's rare to find more
than 20 live lice on any head,

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:38.880
there could be dozens or
even hundreds of dead bodies

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:41.480
lingering on your scalp.

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:42.780
Are you feeling itchy yet?

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:47.320
Perhaps even worse is that
they're a pain to get rid of.

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:50.630
Lice can hold their
breath for eight hours.

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:52.810
So they'll be fine when
you go take a shower

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:53.923
or go for a swim.

00:01:55.060 --> 00:01:56.120
They're also notorious

00:01:56.120 --> 00:01:58.563
for developing resistance to insecticides.

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:03.130
During World War II for example,
militaries dusted millions

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:07.277
of Europeans with DDT to
control lice-borne typhus.

00:02:07.277 --> 00:02:09.840
And thanks to our overuse of it,

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.993
lice grew resistance to the poison.

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:16.170
Even today, we're still seeing
the repercussions from it.

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.950
Many over-the-counter shampoos
and lotions use similar

00:02:18.950 --> 00:02:20.373
killing mechanisms to DDT,

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:24.730
which in some places has
made it easier for lice

00:02:24.730 --> 00:02:27.790
to grow resistant to
these treatments as well.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:30.330
But scientists are striking back.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:33.017
In the last decade,
experts have developed new

00:02:33.017 --> 00:02:34.767
weapons of attack for when initial

00:02:34.767 --> 00:02:36.161
over-the-counter treatments don't work-

00:02:37.197 --> 00:02:41.290
like ivermectin lotion, which
paralyzes lice by disrupting

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:42.523
their nervous systems.

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:45.890
And of course, shaving your
head like the Egyptians

00:02:45.890 --> 00:02:47.703
is a cheap and surefire bet.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:49.980
But let's face it,

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.243
most of us probably
can't pull off that look.

